IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. INVENTORY.
*> Daily stock update. Shortfalls become backorders and stock floors at zero.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT IN-FILE  ASSIGN TO "INPUT.DAT"  ORGANIZATION IS LINE SEQUENTIAL.
    SELECT OUT-FILE ASSIGN TO "OUTPUT.DAT" ORGANIZATION IS LINE SEQUENTIAL.
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD IN-FILE.
    COPY INREC.
FD OUT-FILE.
    COPY OUTREC.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 WS-EOF  PIC X VALUE "N".
01 WS-NET  PIC S9(6).
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-PARA.
    OPEN INPUT IN-FILE OUTPUT OUT-FILE
    PERFORM UNTIL WS-EOF = "Y"
        READ IN-FILE
            AT END MOVE "Y" TO WS-EOF
            NOT AT END PERFORM PROCESS-PARA
        END-READ
    END-PERFORM
    CLOSE IN-FILE OUT-FILE
    STOP RUN.
PROCESS-PARA.
    MOVE IN-SKU TO OUT-SKU
    COMPUTE WS-NET = IN-ON-HAND + IN-RECEIVED - IN-SHIPPED
    IF WS-NET < 0
        COMPUTE OUT-BACKORDER = 0 - WS-NET
        MOVE 0 TO OUT-NEW-ON-HAND
    ELSE
        MOVE 0 TO OUT-BACKORDER
        MOVE WS-NET TO OUT-NEW-ON-HAND
    END-IF
    IF OUT-NEW-ON-HAND <= IN-REORDER
        MOVE "R" TO OUT-FLAG
    ELSE
        MOVE " " TO OUT-FLAG
    END-IF
    WRITE OUT-REC.
